codemap 9
tour feature-collapse-all
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note The document toolbar's 'collapse all' collapses every step of the tour being read that has children, so only the top-level steps remain with +n counts; 'expand all' expands every step. The reader reaches for it to see the shape of a long tour without scrolling past every step. Hide and code state are untouched. It is one toggle (doc-collapse), not a pair: in a run at 1600x1000 'collapse all' and 'expand all' were two identical buttons that never said whether the tour was collapsed. The label names what a press does next and the toggle is drawn on while every step with children is collapsed; with only some collapsed it is off and offers 'collapse all'. The palette keeps both commands (the document scenario runs '>collapse all' from it).

